  "what_it_implies": "PARTIAL SYSTEM. The table is not a list: 23 of 29 rows decompose into two or more slots, no word form occupies two slots, no two letters share a decomposition, and the push series is a regular grid — H1 and H2 both hold. It is not a complete system: row 0's relation clause lies outside the three-slot scheme (C2), and ح/هـ do not form an intensity-only pair because ح carries a second alternative (H4). For the measurement this means a miss bears PARTLY on a generative principle — the دفع series and the pairs H1–H3 describe are regular enough to be one — and partly on independent glosses (rows 4, 6, 9, 12, 18, 24 are single-slot). The verdict changes what a result means, never how it is obtained: the grid is not read by any reading or any judgement."
